; =====================================================================
; Galactose VM BIOS Startup Program (bios.gasm)
; =====================================================================
; This BIOS runs first starting at PC=0, plays an ascending chime,
; writes "BIOS OK" to the screen (using VRAM text mode), and gracefully
; falls through to the main program by not calling HALT.

; --- Step 1: Set Sound Duration ---
PUSH 150        ; 150 ms duration
POP R201        ; R201 is the duration register (dur_reg)

; --- Step 2: Play Note 1 (E5 - 659 Hz) ---
PUSH 659        ; Frequency: 659 Hz (E5)
POP R200        ; R200 is the frequency register (freq_reg, triggers playback)

; Delay to let the first note play before triggering the next
PUSH 180        ; 180 ms sleep delay
POP R255        ; R255 is the timing register (sleeps the thread)

; --- Step 3: Play Note 2 (A5 - 880 Hz) ---
PUSH 880        ; Frequency: 880 Hz (A5)
POP R200        ; Triggers tone playback

PUSH 300        ; 300 ms sleep delay to allow sound to finish
POP R255

; --- Step 4: Write "BIOS OK" to VRAM (default Text Mode) ---
; VRAM automatically draws text sequentially for non-zero bytes.
; We store ASCII values directly to early VRAM addresses.

PUSH 66         ; ASCII 'B'
POP R10
STORE 0 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 0

PUSH 73         ; ASCII 'I'
POP R10
STORE 1 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 1

PUSH 79         ; ASCII 'O'
POP R10
STORE 2 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 2

PUSH 83         ; ASCII 'S'
POP R10
STORE 3 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 3

PUSH 32         ; ASCII ' ' (Space)
POP R10
STORE 4 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 4

PUSH 79         ; ASCII 'O'
POP R10
STORE 5 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 5

PUSH 75         ; ASCII 'K'
POP R10
STORE 6 R10     ; Store at VRAM index 6

; --- BIOS Setup Complete ---
; We purposely do NOT issue HALT here.
; The VM will naturally fall through to run the main program bytecodes.
